cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "Enron Distributed-Clue Deception Benchmark: Cross-Context Privacy Inference in LLM Agents"
abstract: >-
  A fully automated benchmark for conjunctive secret recovery: each case hides one
  deliberate concealment across several individually-innocuous emails buried in real
  Enron mail, retained only when the full clue set reveals the secret while every
  proper subset does not. An adversarial agent must find the evidence in the archive
  and combine it to recover who concealed what from whom.
